<title>JAPAN: Japan May soybean imports up 9.47 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan May soybean imports up 9.47 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in May totalled 391,065 tonnes, up 9.47 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  May 97     Apr 97	May 96</p>
<p> Total imports     391,065    435,993     357,216</p>
<p>Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		  328,880    413,911     302,863</p>
<p> China		  18,100     13,607	14,011</p>
<p> Canada		  2,847	8,466	 3,775</p>
<p> Brazil		 41,195	  nil	36,567</p>
<p>Total imports in the first five months of calendar 1997 reached 2,134,485 tonnes against 2,108,037 tonnes a year earlier. -- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
